@node Introduction
@chapter Introduction

whisper-dvr is a companion package for whisper.el that simplifies the
workflow of transcribing audio files from a digital voice recorder
(DVR).

@section Features

@itemize @bullet
@item
Lists all audio files from your DVR directory
@item
Displays file information (name, size, modification time)
@item
Supports multiple audio formats (MP3, WAV, M4A)
@item
Integrates seamlessly with whisper.el for transcription
@item
Inserts transcription directly at point
@end itemize

@section Requirements

@itemize @bullet
@item
Emacs 27.1 or later
@item
whisper.el (@url{https://github.com/natrys/whisper.el})
@item
A working whisper.cpp installation (handled by whisper.el)
@end itemize

@node Installation
@chapter Installation

@section Using straight.el
@cindex installation, straight.el

@lisp
(use-package whisper-dvr
  :straight (whisper-dvr :type git :host github
                         :repo "MooersLab/whisper-dvr")
  :after whisper
  :bind ("C-c w d" . whisper-dvr))
@end lisp

@section Manual Installation
@cindex installation, manual

@enumerate
@item
Clone the repository:

@example
git clone https://github.com/MooersLab/whisper-dvr.git
@end example

@item
Add to your load-path:

@lisp
(add-to-list 'load-path "/path/to/whisper-dvr")
(require 'whisper-dvr)
@end lisp
@end enumerate

@node Configuration
@chapter Configuration
@cindex configuration

Basic configuration:

@lisp
(setq whisper-dvr-directory "/Volumes/IC RECORDER/REC_FILE/FOLDER01")
(global-set-key (kbd "C-c w d") #'whisper-dvr)
@end lisp

Set the directory to match where your DVR mounts on your system.

@node Usage
@chapter Usage

@section Basic Usage
@cindex usage, basic

@enumerate
@item
Connect your digital voice recorder to your computer.

@item
Open an Emacs buffer where you want the transcription inserted.

@item
Run @kbd{M-x whisper-dvr} or press @kbd{C-c w d}.

@item
Select an audio file from the completion list.

@item
Wait for the transcription to complete.
@end enumerate

@section Changing the DVR Directory
@cindex directory, changing
@findex whisper-dvr-set-directory

If your DVR is mounted at a different location:

@example
M-x whisper-dvr-set-directory RET /path/to/dvr RET
@end example

@section Switching Between the SD Card and the Built-in Memory
@cindex SD card
@cindex memory card
@findex whisper-dvr-set-directory-to-sd-card
@findex whisper-dvr-set-directory-to-internal-memory

Sony recorders keep recordings in two places, the built-in memory and a
removable SD card, and the two use different folder layouts.  Two
commands switch between them without a directory prompt:

@example
M-x whisper-dvr-set-directory-to-sd-card
M-x whisper-dvr-set-directory-to-internal-memory
@end example

Each command copies the matching customization variable into
@code{whisper-dvr-directory}.  A prefix argument saves the value with
@code{customize-save-variable} so that the choice outlives the session:

@example
C-u M-x whisper-dvr-set-directory-to-sd-card
@end example

The directory is set even when the volume is not mounted, so either
command can be run before the recorder is plugged in.

@section Interactive Commands
@cindex commands

@table @code
@item whisper-dvr
@findex whisper-dvr
List audio files from the DVR directory and transcribe the selected file.
Default keybinding: @kbd{C-c w d}.  When @code{whisper-dvr-llm-postprocess} is non-nil, the raw
transcript is then structured by an LLM (@pxref{LLM Post-Processing}).
A prefix argument inverts that setting for one run.

@item whisper-dvr-set-directory
@findex whisper-dvr-set-directory
Interactively set the DVR directory path.

@item whisper-dvr-set-directory-to-sd-card
@findex whisper-dvr-set-directory-to-sd-card
Reset the DVR directory to @code{whisper-dvr-sd-card-directory}.
With a prefix argument, save the value for later sessions.

@item whisper-dvr-set-directory-to-internal-memory
@findex whisper-dvr-set-directory-to-internal-memory
Reset the DVR directory to
@code{whisper-dvr-internal-memory-directory}.
With a prefix argument, save the value for later sessions.

@item whisper-dvr-transcribe-file
@findex whisper-dvr-transcribe-file
Transcribe one audio file without the selection menu.  This is the
entry point used by batch transcription and by the automatic device
handlers.
@end table

@node LLM Post-Processing
@chapter LLM Post-Processing
@cindex LLM post-processing
@cindex transcript-parser skill

whisper.el returns a raw transcript.  When
@code{whisper-dvr-llm-postprocess} is non-nil, whisper-dvr sends that
raw text in the background to a large language model that applies the
transcript-parser skill.  The skill returns a LaTeX fragment with
@code{\subsubsection} headings, @code{\index} keys, one sentence per
line, expanded contractions, corrected grammar, and a closing list of
TODO items.

Think of whisper.el as a court reporter who takes down every word, and
of the LLM as the editor who turns that record into a clean document.
The editor works in a separate process, so Emacs stays responsive.

@section How it works

@enumerate
@item
@code{whisper-dvr} transcribes the selected recording, and whisper.el
inserts the raw text at point.
@item
whisper-dvr captures the text through
@code{whisper-after-transcription-hook} and
@code{whisper-after-insert-hook}.
@item
The text goes to the backend named by @code{whisper-dvr-llm-backend}.
@item
The answer replaces the raw text, follows it, or opens in its own
buffer, according to @code{whisper-dvr-llm-insert-method}.
@end enumerate

The raw transcript is never lost.  A failed or timed out request
leaves it in place.  When the raw text was edited while the model was
working, the result is inserted after it instead of replacing it.

A prefix argument to @code{whisper-dvr} inverts
@code{whisper-dvr-llm-postprocess} for one run.

@section Choosing the model or harness
@cindex backends, LLM
@cindex local models

@table @code
@item claude-code
Claude Code in print mode.  The harness loads the skill named by
@code{whisper-dvr-llm-skill-name} from its own skills directory.

@item anthropic
The Anthropic Messages API through curl.  The body of
@code{whisper-dvr-llm-skill-file} becomes the system prompt.

@item openai-compatible
Any OpenAI style chat completions server.  Ollama, the llama.cpp
server, LM Studio, and vLLM all qualify, so this backend runs the skill
with a local model.

@item command
Any shell command that reads the prompt on standard input and prints
the answer.  Every @samp{%m} in @code{whisper-dvr-llm-command} is
replaced by the model name.

@item function
An Emacs Lisp function called with the instructions, the transcript, a
callback, and an error callback.  This backend suits gptel or ellama.
@end table

@lisp
;; Claude Code as the harness.
(setq whisper-dvr-llm-postprocess t
      whisper-dvr-llm-backend 'claude-code)

;; A local model served by Ollama.
(setq whisper-dvr-llm-backend 'openai-compatible
      whisper-dvr-llm-model "qwen2.5:14b")

;; The Anthropic API.  The key comes from ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or
;; from auth-source for the host api.anthropic.com.
(setq whisper-dvr-llm-backend 'anthropic
      whisper-dvr-llm-model "claude-sonnet-5-5")
@end lisp

@section LLM commands

@table @code
@item whisper-dvr-toggle-llm-postprocess
@findex whisper-dvr-toggle-llm-postprocess
Turn post-processing of new transcripts on or off.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-select-backend
@findex whisper-dvr-llm-select-backend
Choose the backend and the model for the current session.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-process-region
@findex whisper-dvr-llm-process-region
Post-process the active region, or the whole buffer when no region is
active.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-process-file
@findex whisper-dvr-llm-process-file
Read a transcript file such as @file{notes.txt} and write
@file{notes_parsed.tex} beside it.  With a prefix argument, visit the
new file.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-cancel
@findex whisper-dvr-llm-cancel
Cancel every running request.  The raw text stays in place.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-test-backend
@findex whisper-dvr-llm-test-backend
Send a short sample transcript to the configured backend and report
the result.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-show-log
@findex whisper-dvr-llm-show-log
Show the command, exit code, standard error, and standard output of
each LLM run.  Claude Code writes many of its errors to standard
output, so check here when a failure message is unclear.
@end table

@section LLM settings
@cindex customization, LLM

@table @code
@item whisper-dvr-llm-postprocess
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-postprocess
Non-nil sends new transcripts to the LLM.  Default @code{nil}.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-backend
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-backend
The LLM or harness that runs the skill.  Default @code{claude-code}.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-model
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-model
Model name, or @code{nil} for the default in
@code{whisper-dvr-llm-default-models}.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-default-models
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-default-models
Fallback model for each backend.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-api-url
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-api-url
Endpoint for the HTTP backends, or @code{nil} for the default.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-api-key
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-api-key
A string, a function that returns a string, or @code{nil} to read the
environment and then auth-source.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-skill-name
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-skill-name
The skill the harness is asked to run.  Default
@code{"transcript-parser"}.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-skill-file
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-skill-file
The SKILL.md file whose body instructs the other backends.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-default-instructions
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-default-instructions
A condensed copy of the skill used when the skill file is missing.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-claude-program
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-claude-program
Path to Claude Code.  Emacs started from the macOS Dock may need a full
path.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-claude-prompt
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-claude-prompt
The prompt passed to @command{claude -p}.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-claude-args
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-claude-args
Extra arguments for Claude Code.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-claude-unset-env
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-claude-unset-env
Environment variables removed before Claude Code runs.  The default
removes @env{ANTHROPIC_API_KEY}, so Claude Code uses the Pro or Max
subscription login instead of billing an API key.  A ``Credit balance
is too low'' error means the key was used.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-claude-embed-skill
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-claude-embed-skill
Non-nil also passes the skill text with
@option{--append-system-prompt}.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-command
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-command
Command line for the @code{command} backend.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-function
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-function
Function for the @code{function} backend.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-insert-method
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-insert-method
One of @code{replace}, @code{append}, or @code{buffer}.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-output-buffer-name
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-output-buffer-name
Buffer used by the @code{buffer} method.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-timeout
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-timeout
Seconds before a request is abandoned.  Default 900.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-max-tokens
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-max-tokens
Output token limit for the HTTP backends.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-temperature
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-temperature
Sampling temperature, or @code{nil} for the server default.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-curl-program
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-curl-program
Path to curl.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-wait-message
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-wait-message
Notice shown in the echo area while the LLM works.  The default reads
``Please wait, the LLM is parsing the transcript.  This step can take
several minutes.''  Set it to @code{nil} to show nothing.

@item whisper-dvr-llm-after-process-hook
@vindex whisper-dvr-llm-after-process-hook
Functions called with the start and end of the inserted result.
@end table

@node Customization
@chapter Customization

@section whisper-dvr-directory
@vindex whisper-dvr-directory
@cindex customization, directory

The directory path where your DVR stores recordings.

Default: @code{"/Volumes/IC RECORDER/REC_FILE/FOLDER01"}

@lisp
(setq whisper-dvr-directory "/your/dvr/path")
@end lisp

@section whisper-dvr-sd-card-directory
@vindex whisper-dvr-sd-card-directory
@cindex customization, SD card

The directory path where the removable SD card stores recordings.

Default: @code{"/Volumes/MEMORY CARD/private/SONY/REC_FILE/FOLDER01"}

@lisp
(setq whisper-dvr-sd-card-directory
      "/Volumes/MEMORY CARD/private/SONY/REC_FILE/FOLDER01")
@end lisp

@section whisper-dvr-internal-memory-directory
@vindex whisper-dvr-internal-memory-directory
@cindex customization, internal memory

The directory path where the recorder's built-in memory stores
recordings.

Default: @code{"/Volumes/IC RECORDER/REC_FILE/FOLDER01"}

@lisp
(setq whisper-dvr-internal-memory-directory
      "/Volumes/IC RECORDER/REC_FILE/FOLDER01")
@end lisp

@section whisper-dvr-file-extensions
@vindex whisper-dvr-file-extensions
@cindex customization, file extensions

List of audio file extensions to include when listing files.

Default: @code{'("mp3" "wav" "m4a")}

@lisp
(setq whisper-dvr-file-extensions '("mp3" "wav" "m4a" "ogg"))
@end lisp

@node Troubleshooting
@chapter Troubleshooting
@cindex troubleshooting

@section LLM post-processing skipped or failed
@cindex error, LLM

A warning that LLM post-processing was skipped means Emacs could not
find @command{claude}, @command{curl}, or the configured command.  Set
@code{whisper-dvr-llm-claude-program} to a full path.  When a request
fails, the raw transcript stays in the buffer and the message names the
cause, such as an HTTP 401 for a bad key or a timeout for a long
recording on a slow local model.

@section DVR directory does not exist
@cindex error, directory not found

Ensure your DVR is connected and mounted.  Check the mount path with:

@example
ls /Volumes/  # macOS
ls /media/    # Linux
@end example

@section No audio files found
@cindex error, no files found

Verify that:
@itemize @bullet
@item
The directory path is correct
@item
The directory contains files with supported extensions
@item
File permissions allow reading
@end itemize

@section Transcription starts recording instead of transcribing
@cindex error, wrong number of arguments
@cindex whisper-file, API change

This was a bug in versions prior to 0.2.0.  The issue occurred because
@code{whisper-file} in whisper.el changed from accepting a file path
argument to being an interactive-only function.

Update to version 0.2.0 or later, which correctly calls @code{whisper-run}
with the file path directly.

